{
  "_comment": [
    "A standing 'pqp Capacity' dashboard from the 2026-10-22 capacity review (section G, the monitoring gaps):",
    "estimated vs measured SFU load, per-container CPU and memory on the API box, Caddy request rate and 5xx,",
    "and the API event-loop lag. Standard Grafana dashboard JSON model: Dashboards > New > Import, or POST it to",
    "/api/dashboards/db as {dashboard: <this, id: null>, overwrite: true}. Replace <PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>",
    "with the datasource uid (`grafanacloud-prom` on this stack). Nothing here is provisioned from the repo; the",
    "Grafana UI is the source of truth once imported.",
    "WHICH SERIES NEED WHAT, so a 'No data' panel is read correctly:",
    "  pqp_api_sfu_admission_* and pqp_api_event_loop_*  need the updated tools/monitoring exporter on the SFU box",
    "    (the API change that adds the fields is its own PR, restarts-api);",
    "  container_* {box=api-pqp}                          need the new config.alloy loaded on the API box;",
    "  caddy_* {box=api-pqp}                              need the Caddyfile reloaded AND the new config.alloy loaded;",
    "  node_* {box=sfu-pqp}                               already exist.",
    "Default range is 24 hours at 1 minute refresh."
  ],
  "title": "pqp Capacity",
  "uid": "pqp-capacity",
  "tags": [
    "pqp",
    "capacity"
  ],
  "timezone": "utc",
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "time": {
    "from": "now-24h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "refresh": "1m",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "SFU: what the admission budget believes against what the box carries",
      "type": "row",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Estimated vs measured SFU load (Mbit/s)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "Mbits",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "budget (VOICE_PROMOTION_MAX_SFU_MBPS)"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                "value": {
                  "fill": "dash",
                  "dash": [
                    10,
                    10
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "sum(pqp_api_sfu_admission_estimated_mbps{region=\"sao\"})",
          "legendFormat": "estimated (admission estimator, sao)"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(node_network_transmit_bytes_total{box=\"sfu-pqp\"}[5m])) * 8 / 1e6",
          "legendFormat": "measured tx (sfu-pqp, 5m rate)"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "max(pqp_api_sfu_admission_budget_mbps{region=\"sao\"})",
          "legendFormat": "budget (VOICE_PROMOTION_MAX_SFU_MBPS)"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Estimated: the Mbit/s the API prices for the SFU rooms on the home box (cameras and shares only; audio is not priced), from the same estimate an admission compares against the budget. Measured: the box's real transmit rate, everything it sends (audio, video, TURN). They are not meant to be equal: the estimate is deliberately a worst case. What matters is the ratio below and whether the estimate sits at the budget while the box is quiet, which is how 2026-10-20 refused 56 cameras on a box at 32 percent CPU. Needs the exporter deployed on the SFU box (PR with pqp_api_sfu_admission_*) and Alloy's node exporter there."
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Estimated / measured ratio (home box)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 2.5
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "line"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "sum(pqp_api_sfu_admission_estimated_mbps{region=\"sao\"}) / clamp_min(sum(rate(node_network_transmit_bytes_total{box=\"sfu-pqp\"}[5m])) * 8 / 1e6, 1)",
          "legendFormat": "estimated / measured tx"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Above 2.5 for 15 minutes while the box CPU is under 40 percent pages (alert 'SFU admission estimate far above what the box carries'). A healthy room mix sits around the worst-case factor of the estimate; read the first week of data before trusting the line, because the price was recalibrated on 2026-10-21 (sfu_video_price_calibrated, per-box budget). The ratio is noisy below about 20 Mbit/s measured; the alert has a floor for that."
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "title": "SFU box CPU (sfu-pqp)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 40
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 85
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "line"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "100 * (1 - avg(rate(node_cpu_seconds_total{box=\"sfu-pqp\",mode=\"idle\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "CPU busy %"
        }
      ],
      "description": "The other half of the 2026-10-20 story: the estimate was at the budget while this read about 32 percent."
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "title": "Estimated load by region (Mbit/s)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "Mbits",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": ".*budget"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                "value": {
                  "fill": "dash",
                  "dash": [
                    10,
                    10
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "pqp_api_sfu_admission_estimated_mbps",
          "legendFormat": "{{region}} estimated"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "pqp_api_sfu_admission_budget_mbps",
          "legendFormat": "{{region}} budget"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Every region the estimator knows, including mia and lhr when LIVEKIT_REGIONS names them. region=all means sfu_video_budget_per_box is off and one number covers the cluster. To divide a regional estimate by its box, use node_network_transmit_bytes_total{box=\"sfu-mia\"} once install-regional.sh has run there."
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "title": "Admission checks and refusals (5 min window)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 10
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": ".*refused"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "red"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (region) (pqp_api_sfu_admission_checks_5m)",
          "legendFormat": "{{region}} checks"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (region) (pqp_api_sfu_admission_refusals_5m)",
          "legendFormat": "{{region}} refused"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Camera, share and mesh-promotion decisions against the budget, summed across both API replicas. Refusals above zero while the box CPU panel is low is the 2026-10-20 shape."
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "title": "API box: which container is using the box",
      "type": "row",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 18
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "title": "CPU per container (cores)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 19
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (service) (rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total{box=\"api-pqp\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "cAdvisor inside Alloy on the API box. 1 is one full core of the box's 4. api-a and api-b should track each other; one far above the other is a hot replica, which host CPU cannot show."
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "title": "Memory per container (working set)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 19
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "max by (service) (container_memory_working_set_bytes{box=\"api-pqp\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "What the OOM killer counts (usage minus inactive file cache). The box has 8 GiB."
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "title": "Container restarts (last hour)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 19
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (service) (changes(container_start_time_seconds{box=\"api-pqp\"}[1h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "A rolling deploy shows one step per replica. A container that steps repeatedly with no deploy is crash-looping (an OOM kill shows here before any alert would)."
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "title": "Caddy: what the API box serves",
      "type": "row",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 27
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "title": "Request rate (req/s)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(caddy_http_request_duration_seconds_count{box=\"api-pqp\",handler!=\"metrics\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "requests/s"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Everything Caddy finished serving on api.pqp.gg. A WebSocket counts once, when it closes, so this is an HTTP-shaped number, not a socket count."
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "title": "5xx responses",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 28
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(caddy_http_request_duration_seconds_count{box=\"api-pqp\",handler!=\"metrics\",code=~\"5..\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "5xx per second"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (code) (rate(caddy_http_request_duration_seconds_count{box=\"api-pqp\",handler!=\"metrics\",code=~\"5..\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{code}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "502 and 503 are Caddy failing to reach an API replica or a replica answering database_unavailable. During a rolling deploy a few 502s are expected for under 10 seconds (the health check pulls a replica out of rotation every 5 s). Sustained 5xx is not."
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "title": "In flight and upstream health",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 28
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "sum(caddy_http_requests_in_flight{box=\"api-pqp\",handler!=\"metrics\"})",
          "legendFormat": "in flight (about open sockets)"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "caddy_reverse_proxy_upstreams_healthy{box=\"api-pqp\"}",
          "legendFormat": "healthy {{upstream}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "In flight is mostly open /ws connections (Caddy proxies them for their whole life). Healthy upstream is 1 per replica; api-b reads 0 when the box runs API_REPLICAS=1."
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "title": "API process: is a replica's thread stalled",
      "type": "row",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 36
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "title": "Event-loop lag, worst replica (ms)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 37
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ms",
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 100
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 200
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "line"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "pqp_api_event_loop_lag_p50_ms",
          "legendFormat": "p50"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "pqp_api_event_loop_lag_p99_ms",
          "legendFormat": "p99"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "pqp_api_event_loop_lag_max_ms",
          "legendFormat": "max"
        }
      ],
      "description": "How late the API process fires its own timers, over the last minute, with the 20 ms sampling floor already subtracted: a healthy process reads 0 to 2. p99 is the worst 5 s slice's p99. The alert fires at p99 above 200 ms for 5 minutes. A stall holds ONE replica's thread while host CPU reads 20 percent, so this is the number the pool and the box CPU cannot give. Worst of the two replicas."
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "title": "Event-loop lag against sockets",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 37
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "open sockets (this process)"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.axisPlacement",
                "value": "right"
              },
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "short"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "pqp_api_event_loop_lag_p99_ms",
          "legendFormat": "p99 lag (ms)"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "<PROMETHEUS_DATASOURCE_UID>"
          },
          "expr": "pqp_api_sockets",
          "legendFormat": "open sockets (this process)"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Does lag climb with the socket count (a fan-out cost that scales with people) or arrive on its own (one slow handler)? Sockets are per scraped process, so read the shape rather than the level."
    }
  ]
}
